s\": [\"/PWM1\", \"/PWM1_C2\"], \"observed\": \"No R10 appears in the netlist, so the jumper that should connect /PWM1 to bus pin 21 is absent.\", \"expected\": \"A 0 \u03a9 jumper R10 between /PWM1 and /PWM1_C2, as referenced by the schematic note \\\"Short R10, R10 for Core2 and CoreS3\\\".\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"22\\\") (name \\\"/PWM1\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\")\\n      (node (ref \\\"C6\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\\n      (node (ref \\\"R3\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\\n      (node (ref \\\"R9\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\"}, {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"Short R10, R10 for Core2 and CoreS3 / Short R9, R11 for others\"}], \"impact\": \"The Core2/CoreS3 PWM1 route is not connected through a jumper. Combined with C6 it produces the AC-coupled, distorted signal described above.\", \"confidence\": 0.5}], \"summary\": \"The channel-1 jumper position that should be R10 (0 \u03a9, linking /PWM1 to bus pin 21) is instead a 100 \u00b5F capacitor, C6, which AC-couples the PWM1 servo signal. This is the main deviation from the specified design.\"}",
